                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <span>NEXT PERIOD</span>
                        <strong>AFTER THE KEYBLADE WAR</strong>
                    </div>

                </div>

            </section>


            <!-- HISTORICAL SIGNIFICANCE -->

            <section class="database-section">

                <div class="database-heading">
                    HISTORICAL SIGNIFICANCE
                </div>

                <p>
                    This period represents the foundation of the
                    recorded history of the Keyblade wielders.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The decisions made by the Master of Masters and
                    his apprentices established the conditions that
                    produced the first great collapse of the world.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The survival of selected Keyblade wielders ensured
                    that the light and the Keyblade legacy would
                    continue beyond the destruction of the original
                    world.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The events of this period would also establish
                    the foundations for conflicts that would continue
                    for generations.
                </p>

            </section>


            <!-- RECORD STATUS -->

            <section class="database-section">

                <div class="database-heading">
                    RECORD STATUS
                </div>

                <p>
                    This record is classified as
                    <strong>CONFIRMED / COMPLETE</strong>.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The historical sequence is documented through
                    records concerning the Master of Masters, the
                    Foretellers, Luxu, the Unions and the Dandelions.
                </p>

            </section>


